# Pin JSON to LF line endings. The datagen writes LF (Java `\n`) and
# scripts/copy_assets_to_common.py copies that output byte-for-byte into
# common/src/main/resources. With the system core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows),
# git would otherwise check JSON out as CRLF, so every :fabric:runDatagen dirties
# thousands of files with pure line-ending churn. eol=lf overrides that so the two agree.
*.json text eol=lf

# Pin Markdown to LF too. Both port branches (port/1.20.1, port/1.21.1) carry a
# copy of docs/backport-pass2/, and the two worktrees were checking the same
# markdown out differently — one CRLF, one LF — so diffing them reported six
# "divergent" files, three of which differed by nothing but the trailing \r.
# The stored blobs already matched (core.autocrlf=true stores LF); this rule only
# settles the working-tree side so a cross-worktree diff means something.
*.md text eol=lf
